## Migration Strategy

### Step 1: Vertebra migration creates generic tables

New SQL migration `007_generic_documents.sql` under `backend/src/modules/vertebra/migrations/acopio_materia_prima/`:

```sql
-- Migración 007: reemplaza acopio_document_type_catalog + acopio_entry_documents
-- con las tablas genéricas del motor de documentos.

-- Tabla genérica del catálogo
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS document_type_catalog (...);

-- Tabla genérica de documentos
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS entry_documents (...);
```

This runs inside the vertebra migration processor — same mechanism as migrations 001-006.

### Step 2: Seed acopio document types in new table

New SQL `008_seed_acopio_document_types.sql`: copies the existing document types from `005_pota_document_types.sql` (adapted to the new schema — `vertebra_code` column, `validation_rules` as array, `context_conditions` instead of `required_for`).

**Idempotent**: all INSERTs use `ON CONFLICT (vertebra_code, code) DO UPDATE`.

### Step 3: Drop old tables

`009_drop_legacy_document_tables.sql`:
```sql
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS acopio_entry_documents;
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS acopio_document_type_catalog;
```

Only runs AFTER step 1 and 2 are confirmed in staging. Safe because DB is empty in production.

### Order

Migrations run in numeric order by the vertebra migration processor (existing mechanism). Order: 007 → 008 → 009.

**Idempotence**: all CREATE TABLE use `IF NOT EXISTS`, all INSERTs use `ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE`, all DROPs use `IF EXISTS`. Safe to re-run.

