## Risks & Mitigations

| Severity | Risk | Mitigation |
|----------|------|------------|
| CRITICAL | Accidentally writing to `trace_event_log` from engine | Code review enforced: DocumentEngineModule has zero direct dep on trace module. Integration test asserts no trace rows created after extraction. |
| CRITICAL | `ai_extracted_json` overwritten (losing original) | Write-once guard in service: if `ai_extracted_json IS NOT NULL`, reject write. Only callback writes it; human correction goes to `human_corrected_json`. |
| MAJOR | BullMQ job lost on worker crash before n8n responds | `extraction_status = EXTRACTING` on job start. On worker restart, a recovery job (on module init or scheduled) can re-queue documents stuck in EXTRACTING for > 30 min. |
| MAJOR | Context resolver returns null for `equals` rule | Engine must treat resolver null as "cannot evaluate" → rule skipped (not failed). Semaphore does NOT go RED on unresolvable context. Log a warning. |
| MAJOR | n8n workflow not updated to use new callback URL | Migration guide: update `backendUrl` variable in n8n workflow. Old `/acopio/n8n-callback` forwards for one release cycle. |
| MODERATE | `documents-admin.controller.ts` references non-existent fields | Fix as part of this change (remove or remap broken references). |
| MODERATE | `context_conditions` semantics opaque across vertebras | Documented contract: engine passes the raw value to the resolver. Each vertebra interprets its own conditions. This is intentional — not a bug. |
| LOW | Migration 007-009 ordering | Processor reads directory entries sorted numerically. Files named 007/008/009 run in correct order automatically. |
